#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0369 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE 82-RULE GENERATOR-WILDCARD POPULATION (Fix #331 finding; owner ruled 2026-08-22 that all 82 are BUCKET 1 - no rule edit - with a sample of fixtures owed by the closing lane; authored by Fix #340). These rules never carried the injected var_exists guard in rules/ (NonEmptyGuardInliner.isGeneratorWildcard excludes wildcard names), but WildcardExpander re-ran installNativeExpr on the EXPANDED rule, where the arm wrapped the now-concrete leaf - so before Fix #330 an absent primary column silenced them at runtime. With the arm retired the expanded leaf is a bare empty(X): absent = all-missing, TRUE on every row. The mirror: the imputation-flag column ADTF is the absent one. The root 'A' is raised off the declared ADT, and not empty(ADTF) is FALSE on every row of an absent column, so the rule is correctly silent even though ADTM is absent too. The restricting conjunct is what makes this bucket 1."
# Declared-tier scope: the class= declaration disagrees with the columns, so #define must
# carry it to RuleRunner (ScenarioDeclaredScopeProvider.install).
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col ADT type=Num
